{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5347186","formula":"C₂₀H₂₃NO₄","hill":"C20H23NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Efaproxiral"},"descriptions":{"en":"Efaproxiral (INN) is an analogue of bezafibrate [a lipid-lowering agent], developed for the treatment of depression, traumatic brain injury, ischemia, stroke, myocardial infarction, diabetes, hypoxia, sickle cell disease, hypercholesterolemia and as a radio sensitiser. The chemical is a derivative of propanoic acid. One use for efaproxiral is to increase the efficacy of certain chemotherapy drugs which have reduced efficacy against hypoxic tumours, and can thus be made more effective by increased offloading of oxygen into the tumour tissues."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":122335,"mass":341.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1=CC(=CC(=C1)NC(=O)CC2=CC=C(C=C2)OC(C)(C)C(=O)O)C","inchikey":"BNFRJXLZYUTIII-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-[4-[2-(3,5-dimethylanilino)-2-oxoethyl]phenoxy]-2-methylpropanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"122335","atoms":48,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.513,"y":0.436,"z":0.327,"el":"O"},{"x":-6.555,"y":-2.508,"z":0.214,"el":"O"},{"x":-7.01,"y":-0.327,"z":0.608,"el":"O"},{"x":1.633,"y":0.655,"z":-1.77,"el":"O"},{"x":2.771,"y":1.18,"z":0.215,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.715,"y":-0.958,"z":0.092,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.858,"y":-1.734,"z":1.087,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.334,"y":-1.253,"z":-1.356,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.643,"y":1.856,"z":-0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.238,"y":0.904,"z":0.17,"el":"C"},{"x":0.748,"y":2.367,"z":-0.323,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.199,"y":-1.203,"z":0.333,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.521,"y":1.847,"z":-1.234,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.065,"y":1.388,"z":1.093,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.822,"y":1.37,"z":-1.073,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.366,"y":0.911,"z":1.254,"el":"C"},{"x":3.88,"y":0.301,"z":0